  "open_observations": [
    "file-graphs/ is ~670k files / 2.6 GB in production; confirm graph_gc.py caps it.",
    "Feedback loop (pipeline 9) is idle in production: 4 shadow_routes, empty proposals, no changelog/pinned_rules/tune_state files. Root cause: shadow_log.py used a positional hwm index (2105) past the 1000-line read_events() window, skipping every new row; fixed with a timestamp cursor (hwm_ts) in state.",
    "Dormant (flagged \"prod\": \"absent\" in data_file_cross_reference, written only by code paths that have not fired): pinned_rules.json, tune_state.json, routing_changelog.json, policy_changelog.jsonl, calibration.jsonl, signal.jsonl, stale_refresh.json, file_graph_refresh_stats.json.",
    "reward_events.jsonl never created in production although reward_signal events are routed there by design; reward_log.jsonl is the live ledger.",
    "calibration.jsonl, signal.jsonl, stale_refresh.json, file_graph_refresh_stats.json, semantic_role_alignment.jsonl are written by code paths that have not fired in production.",
    "Write-only files with no reader in scripts/: counterfactual_log.jsonl, worker_response_violations.jsonl, claude_classifier.jsonl, perturbation_benchmark.json - decide whether to add a consumer or drop the writer.",
    "The hooks.json PostToolUse/Write chain does not call session_summary.py; it is a library used by session_hook.py.",
    "Pipeline 9 produces no proposals: shadow_evaluation.json shows candidate_expected_reward 0.0 for all 10 rules (actual_mean_reward 1.0, improvement_delta -1.0, selection_bias_warning true). Candidate roles are only logged as hypotheticals and never executed, so there is no candidate reward data. Cause of the 0.0: shadow_evaluator.py compute_rule_evaluation looked up candidate history under (rule_id, candidate_role), e.g. ('DIRECT:qa_simple', 'FW'), but composite rule_ids lead with the actual role so that key never exists. Fixed 2026-10-04 to use '<candidate_role>:<intent>' with a legacy-key fallback; re-check shadow_evaluation.json and policy_proposals.json after a few sessions on the resynced build."
  ]
